    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1022">

                <pb facs="1131" n="1035" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1035"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Woodford to Mr. Sherman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-08"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 170.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    this day of Department dispatch No. 139, dated February 24, 1898, instructing
                    me, at the request of the Secretary of the Navy, to express to the Spanish
                    Government his high appreciation of the services rendered and honors paid by the
                    Cuban authorities to the officers and men of the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Maine</hi> on the occasion of the public funeral of the
                    members of the crew lost in the disaster.</p>
                <p>I have this day addressed an official communication to the Spanish minister of
                    foreign affairs, expressing such appreciation.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stewart L. Woodford.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
